Aim
To understand Python loops and automate the inspection and classification of manufactured parts.

Objectives
Generate 10 random part diameters (IT12).

Classify 100 parts into ACCEPT, REWORK and SCRAP categories (IT10).

Use break and continue to control inspection (IT8).

Use a while loop to achieve five consecutive ACCEPT results with a safety limit of 500 attempts (IT6).

Concepts Used
For loop

While loop

If-elif-else statements

Break and continue

Random number generation

Counter variables

Working Principle
ACCEPT: Diameter between 24.95 mm and 25.05 mm.

REWORK: Diameter outside acceptance limits but within 24.90 mm to 25.10 mm.

SCRAP: Diameter outside 24.90 mm to 25.10 mm.

Observations
Random diameters are generated automatically.

Each part is classified according to tolerance limits.

Counters maintain the number of accepted, rework and scrap parts.

Loops reduce manual inspection work.

A safety limit prevents infinite execution.

Result
Successfully studied and implemented Python loops for automated part inspection, classification and production reporting.

Conclusion
Python loops help automate repetitive production tasks, reduce manual effort and improve inspection efficiency
